], with expected values computed from [artifact:prj-dbb4754f2d.interface-spec.a1] and not read from the RTL. It serves [requirement:req-91ad500fdf]. Every compare increments either the pass count or the fail count. The verdict line uses the run nonce read from a plusarg. The testbench also counts a failure when the nonce plusarg is missing or a coverage minimum is missed.", "entry": "crc8_block_tb"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["The hand-computed anchor values (reload then byte 0x00 -> crc 0x0C, 0xFF -> 0xFF, 0x80 -> 0x85, 0x01 -> 0x0B) and table anchors (tbl[0x01]=0x07, tbl[0x80]=0x89, tbl[0x7F]=0x7A, tbl[0xFF]=0xF3) were derived by hand from spec section 2.2 and cross-checked by polynomial linearity; they have not been simulated.", "The name of the nonce plusarg is not given in my inputs. The testbench tries NIRMAAN_NONCE=, nirmaan_nonce=, NONCE= and nonce= in turn. If the platform uses a different name, the verdict line carries NONCE_MISSING and the run fails.", "The corner-count minimums were chosen from expected-value estimates for the fixed seed. I have not confirmed by a run that this seed reaches them.", "No simulation, lint or mutant run has been performed by me; the platform's simulator.run over this file is still to come."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Timing: inputs change on the falling edge and outputs are sampled 1 ns after the rising edge, so the testbench does not race the design. The model update order (reset, then init, then valid, else hold) follows spec section 2.1 and 2.2 clause order. Mutants this testbench should catch: a wrong start value (anchors and reset checks), a wrong polynomial (anchors and the scoreboard), a missing final inversion (CRC-EMPTY after reset), reflected byte order (anchors 0x80 and 0x01), init losing to valid (directed D3 and the random init-with-valid count) and a broken hold (D4). Main risk: the unconfirmed nonce plusarg name. If the first platform run reports NONCE_MISSING, the tech lead should supply the platform'